</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Default inference configuration</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unless otherwise specified, we use <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=3</annotation></semantics></math> hospital agents and retrieve one local case per hospital, giving three retrieved cases per cross-hospital diagnosis instance. We set <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=32</annotation></semantics></math> latent positions per hospital block. Decoding uses greedy generation with temperature <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. All methods use the single-answer output format in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Diagnosis output format ‣ Appendix C Baselines and Prompt Templates ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Training hyperparameters</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The latent interface is trained with diagnosis cross-entropy on the public training split under the simulated hospital partitions. Table <a href="#A4.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ D.3 Training hyperparameters ‣ Appendix D Training and Implementation Details ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> lists the main hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T9" class="ltx_table">
<table id="A4.T9.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T9.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T9.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt">Hyperparameter</th>
<td id="A4.T9.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Value</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T9.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T9.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Optimizer</th>
<td id="A4.T9.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">AdamW</td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T9.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T9.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning rate</th>
<td id="A4.T9.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="A4.T9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1\times 10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1\times 10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T9.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T9.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Weight decay</th>
