</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Cross-family projector training</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For cross-family deployment, each host uses a jointly trained projector set containing one projector for each non-host encoder family. Each projector maps encoder-side latent hidden states to host-side input embeddings, as described in §<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 MedLatentDx-X: Cross-Family Latent Alignment ‣ 3 Method ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. The encoder LLM backbones, encoder-side distillers, and host LLM backbone remain frozen. Only the projectors and boundary embeddings are updated. Full training details are provided in Appendix <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Cross-Family Deployment Details ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Training data and hardware</h3>

<div id="A4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The latent interface is trained centrally on the public <math id="A4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7{,}220" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7,220</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7{,}220</annotation></semantics></math>-case training split under the controlled five-hospital partition. Validation and test cases are disjoint from training and are never used to update the latent interface. All training and evaluation runs use a single NVIDIA H100 80GB GPU.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Communication Footprint</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We quantify the communication footprint of compact latent blocks relative to prompt-length KV exchange. For a bf16 KV cache with <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> layers, transmitted length <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>, and per-layer KV dimension <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{KV}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>KV</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{KV}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the transmitted size per hospital is</p>
<table id="A5.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Size}(T)=2\cdot L\cdot T\cdot d_{\mathrm{KV}}\cdot 2\;\text{bytes}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Size</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>T</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>KV</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>bytes</mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Size}(T)=2\cdot L\cdot T\cdot d_{\mathrm{KV}}\cdot 2\;\text{bytes},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the first factor of <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> accounts for keys and values, and the last factor of <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of bytes per bf16 element. <span id="A5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Raw KV</span> transmits the full prompt-length cache with <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, while <span id="A5.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx</span> transmits only <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=32</annotation></semantics></math> latent positions. The relative KV communication cost is therefore <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m/T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m/T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for each backbone.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A5.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ Appendix E Communication Footprint ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> reports the measured footprint using each backbone’s own tokenizer and KV geometry. The average local prompt lengths are <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}=162.4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>162.4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}=162.4</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3-4B</span>, <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="184.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>184.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">184.0</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A5.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.2-3B</span>, and <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="189.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>189.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">189.3</annotation></semantics></math> for <span id="A5.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MediPhi</span>. Under these measured lengths, <span id="A5.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx</span> transmits only <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="17" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>17</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">17</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20\%</annotation></semantics></math> of the prompt-length KV cache per hospital, corresponding to a <math id="A5.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A5.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="6\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6\times</annotation></semantics></math> reduction relative to <span id="A5.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Raw KV</span>. At the <math id="A5.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math>-token prompt cap, the relative size is <math id="A5.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32/320=10\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>320</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32/320=10\%</annotation></semantics></math>, or a <math id="A5.p2.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="10\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10\times</annotation></semantics></math> reduction. Text and structured baselines transmit different object types and are therefore listed for access-pattern comparison rather than byte-level equivalence.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.T11" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 11: </span><span id="A5.T11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Communication footprint per hospital.</span> KV-cache sizes are computed in bf16 using each backbone’s measured average local prompt length <math id="A5.T11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and KV geometry. <span id="A5.T11.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx</span> transmits <math id="A5.T11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=32</annotation></semantics></math> latent positions, while <span id="A5.T11.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Raw KV</span> transmits the full prompt-length cache. Relative size is computed as <math id="A5.T11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m/T_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m/T_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
