</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Cross-Family Deployment Details</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix expands the cross-family variant <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx-X</span> (§<a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 MedLatentDx-X: Cross-Family Latent Alignment ‣ 3 Method ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>) and the heterogeneity evaluation (§<a href="#S4.SS5" title="4.5 Cross-Family Deployment ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>). In this setting, hospitals may use different LLM families, such as <span id="A6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3-4B</span>, <span id="A6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.2-3B</span>, and <span id="A6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MediPhi</span>. Because their hidden dimensions and representation statistics differ, non-host latent blocks are mapped into the host space by lightweight projectors <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while same-family blocks are consumed directly.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Components.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a host family <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx-X</span> uses three frozen components and one trainable component.
<span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(i) Per-family distiller.</span> Each family <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math> has a frozen distiller <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> that compresses a hospital’s local prompt into <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m{=}32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m{=}32</annotation></semantics></math> compact latent positions in family <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>’s space.
<span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(ii) Cross-family projector.</span> For each foreign family <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, a trainable projector <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> maps a latent block <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m,d_{\mathcal{E}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m,d_{\mathcal{E}}]</annotation></semantics></math> into the host embedding space <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m,d_{\mathcal{H}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m,d_{\mathcal{H}}]</annotation></semantics></math>. It is implemented as token-wise <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{LayerNorm}(d_{\mathcal{E}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>LayerNorm</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{LayerNorm}(d_{\mathcal{E}})</annotation></semantics></math> followed by a bias-free <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Linear}(d_{\mathcal{E}},d_{\mathcal{H}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Linear</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Linear}(d_{\mathcal{E}},d_{\mathcal{H}})</annotation></semantics></math>.
<span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">(iii) Boundary embeddings.</span> Each latent block is wrapped with learned <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\textsc{bop}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">bop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\textsc{bop}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>/<math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle\textsc{eop}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">eop</mtext><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle\textsc{eop}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> embeddings before host-side consumption.
Same-family hospitals bypass the projector because their latent blocks are already in host space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Latent-cache construction.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since HPO retrieval is deterministic, foreign-family latents are precomputed once per family. For each family <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}</annotation></semantics></math>, every hospital retrieves from its fixed private database using cosine HPO retrieval (Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B HPO-Based Local Retrieval ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>), and the retrieved context is encoded into a stored latent block. Each cache entry maps a <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\text{case\_id},\text{hospital\_id}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mtext>case_id</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>hospital_id</mtext><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\text{case\_id},\text{hospital\_id}\}</annotation></semantics></math> key to a bf16 tensor of shape <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m{=}32,d_{\mathcal{E}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m{=}32,d_{\mathcal{E}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, with boundary tokens enabled and maximum prompt length <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math>. With five hospital databases, the cache contains <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="36{,}100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>36,100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">36{,}100</annotation></semantics></math> training, <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,005</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}005</annotation></semantics></math> validation, and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2{,}005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2,005</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2{,}005</annotation></semantics></math> test entries. Because hospital databases are fixed, the same cache supports any <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Universal joint projector training.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For each host family, we jointly train a universal projector set containing one projector for each foreign encoder family, rather than training each foreign-to-host projector in isolation. We fix <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> and sample each hospital’s family from the host-specific family pool. Native hospitals use the host distiller, while foreign hospitals use their family cache and projector <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We ensure that each batch contains at least one foreign hospital so every projector receives gradient updates. Training minimizes the host’s next-token cross-entropy on the <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">&lt;answer&gt;{disease}&lt;/answer&gt;</span> target, identical to Eq. <a href="#S3.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ Training objective. ‣ 3.2 MedLatentDx-H: Same-Backbone Latent Distillation ‣ 3 Method ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. All LLM backbones and distillers remain frozen. Only projectors and boundary embeddings are updated. Hyperparameters are listed in Table <a href="#A6.T12" title="Table 12 ‣ Universal joint projector training. ‣ Appendix F Cross-Family Deployment Details ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T12" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 12: </span><span id="A6.T12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Universal cross-family projector training.</span> One projector set is trained per host family and reused across hospital compositions.</figcaption>
<div id="A6.T12.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:183.2pt;vertical-align:-88.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(13.1pt,-7.0pt) scale(1.08230413552698,1.08230413552698) ;">
<table id="A6.T12.4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Hyperparameter</th>
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Value</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Latent block <math id="A6.T12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">32</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Hospitals <math id="A6.T12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">3 (fixed)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Epochs</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">3 (<math id="A6.T12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5{,}415" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>5,415</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5{,}415</annotation></semantics></math> steps; <math id="A6.T12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}805" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,805</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}805</annotation></semantics></math>/epoch)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Optimizer</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">AdamW, lr <math id="A6.T12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A6.T12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.01</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.01</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">LR schedule</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">linear, <math id="A6.T12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> warmup steps</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Gradient clip</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><math id="A6.T12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Effective batch</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><math id="A6.T12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> (micro-batch <math id="A6.T12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>, accumulation <math id="A6.T12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Precision</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">bfloat16</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Max prompt / target length</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><math id="A6.T12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="320" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>320</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">320</annotation></semantics></math> / <math id="A6.T12.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>64</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">64</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Retrieval</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">cosine HPO</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Boundary tokens</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">enabled</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Validation</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">every <math id="A6.T12.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="400" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>400</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">400</annotation></semantics></math> steps, <math id="A6.T12.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="128" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>128</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">128</annotation></semantics></math> samples</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T12.4.1.14" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T12.4.1.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">Frozen</th>
<td id="A6.T12.4.1.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;">both backbones and both distillers</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Deployment and inference.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">A host uses its universal projector set. For an <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>-hospital query, each hospital encodes its retrieved case and query phenotypes into a <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[m,d_{\mathcal{E}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[m,d_{\mathcal{E}}]</annotation></semantics></math> latent block. Native blocks come from the host distiller, while foreign blocks come from <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{\mathcal{E}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{\mathcal{E}}</annotation></semantics></math> and are projected to host space by <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{\mathcal{E}\to\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The host concatenates the boundary-wrapped blocks through input embeddings and generates the diagnosis. No per-composition retraining or projector swapping is needed.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation protocol.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Table <a href="#S4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 4.3 Diagnostic Utility ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, we set <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N{=}3</annotation></semantics></math>, with the host as hospital <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and two remote hospitals. Degree <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> is homogeneous, Degree <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> has one foreign remote family, and Degree <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math> has two distinct foreign families. The compositions are Q:L:Q and Q:L:M for the <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3-4B</span> host, and L:Q:L and L:Q:M for the <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.2-3B</span> host, where Q, L, and M denote <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Qwen3-4B</span>, <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Llama-3.2-3B</span>, and <span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MediPhi</span>. Inference uses greedy decoding, temperature <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, seed <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>42</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42</annotation></semantics></math>, and the five-hospital cosine caches. We report accuracy, macro F1, and LLM-as-judge score on the <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="401" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>401</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">401</annotation></semantics></math>-case test set.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Additional Diagnostic Utility Results</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A7.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ Appendix G Additional Diagnostic Utility Results ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> reports diagnostic utility for the medically pretrained <span id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MediPhi</span> host under the same protocol as the main results. The results follow the main-table trend: <span id="A7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx</span> achieves the best overall accuracy, macro F1, and judge score among the compared methods.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.T13" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 13: </span><span id="A7.T13.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Diagnostic utility on <span id="A7.T13.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CrossRare-Bench</span> for the <span id="A7.T13.6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MediPhi</span> host.</span> Same protocol as Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Joint projector training. ‣ 3.3 MedLatentDx-X: Cross-Family Latent Alignment ‣ 3 Method ‣ MedLatentDx: Latent Multi-Agent Communication for Cross-Hospital Rare-Disease Diagnosis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Within the block, <span id="A7.T13.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span> marks the best and <span id="A7.T13.8" class="ltx_text ltx_underline">underline</span> the second best per column; <span id="A7.T13.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-bg-color:#FFF1F5;">pink cells</span> are our method.</figcaption>
