<figure id="A7.T14" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 14: </span><span id="A7.T14.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Trained bottleneck control.</span> <span id="A7.T14.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">MLP-Pool32</span> uses the same diagnosis supervision and latent budget as <span id="A7.T14.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx</span>, but replaces autoregressive latent distillation with mean pooling followed by an MLP projection. Its weak performance suggests that supervised training alone does not explain the gains of <span id="A7.T14.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">MedLatentDx</span>.</figcaption>
