<figure id="A9.T18" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 18: </span><span id="A9.T18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Skewed Dirichlet hospital partition.</span> We use a disease-skewed Dirichlet allocation with <math id="A9.T18.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.3</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A9.T18.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=5</annotation></semantics></math> hospitals. The partition is non-uniform at the disease level while keeping total case counts moderately balanced.</figcaption>
